#
# The card's optional file.  THIS IS A TEMPLATE, the other boards' in every
# line but one: boards/arty-z7-20/linux/mksd-buildroot.sh, run with
# BOARD_DIR=boards/kria-kr260, writes uEnv.txt from it, filling the serverip
# line below from SERVERIP in boards/kria-kr260/linux/local.conf ---
# gitignored, because a machine's address on a private network is not part
# of the project --- and dropping the line when local.conf does not set it.
#
# WHAT IT DECIDES.  The card's boot.scr boots from the card by default: the
# tree, Image, the root filesystem and cadr.bit out of the kria-kr260/ folder
# on the FAT partition, no network needed.  If this file sets `serverip`, it
# takes the network path instead: `dhcp`, fetch kria-kr260/uEnv.net from
# that server, and run the netcmd it defines, which fetches the same four
# files over TFTP from /srv/tftp/kria-kr260.  This file stays at the root of
# the partition beside boot.scr.
#
# **NO `ethaddr` LINE, WHICH IS THE ONE DIFFERENCE.**  This board's MACs are
# its own: the factory U-Boot reads them from the module's EEPROM into
# `ethaddr` and `eth1addr`, and hands `eth1addr` to the J10C port, GEM1, the
# one this project uses.  A card that set `ethaddr` would move GEM0's address
# and nothing else.  So ETHADDR in local.conf does nothing on this board.
serverip=@SERVERIP@

# 1468 rather than the 512-byte default (RFC 2348).  Harmless on the card path.
tftpblocksize=1468
